      "message": "feat(mintinfo): add supportedMethods(op) to list usable mint/melt methods (#673)\n\n* feat(mintinfo): add supportedMethods(op) to list usable mint/melt methods\n\nAdds a convenience for discovering what a consumer can mint or melt with:\n`MintInfo.supportedMethods('mint' | 'melt')` returns the advertised method-unit\nsettings (SwapMethod[]), or [] when the operation is disabled.\n\nThis is the discovery counterpart to the existing point-check\n`supportsMintMeltMethod(op, method, unit)`. Unlike `isSupported(4|5).params`,\nit is operation-named and excludes disabled operations, so \"supported\" means\nusable. Kept on MintInfo only (no Wallet wrapper) to match the existing\nmethod-query surface and avoid a duplicate entry point.\n\n* docs(usage): add Inspect Mint Capabilities recipe for the method-query API\n\nNew usage page documenting how to discover what a mint supports via\nwallet.getMintInfo(): supportedMethods(op) to list usable mint/melt methods,\nsupportsMintMeltMethod(op, method, unit) for a single check, and isSupported(num)\nfor raw NUT support. Adds it to the usage index and cross-links it from the\nCreate Wallet recipe.",
      "tree": {
        "sha": "40d824f192f43e7550c98af4c376a4f950309837",
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/cashubtc/cashu-ts/git/trees/40d824f192f43e7550c98af4c376a4f950309837"
      },
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/cashubtc/cashu-ts/git/commits/9be2d56346ec2b747655c4db65006be79c8f9861",
      "comment_count": 0,
      "verification": {
        "verified": true,
        "reason": "valid",
        "signature": "-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqEGGXCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAepUQAAxDwcUl8ztOQR2MU4KeWO2Y\nObZATaCUmSWD+bKf3RJnbbo7HAaKavz+pCV+H5vQbDh0BysBoSNJsWvRVklu0GfE\nKy7ty1CIO7S/iycWCOrcjWDPMxGIsFSua46qrt6fMf+Ms9OTptvQoPSR6MtMDc5O\nkUutmjIYEPwPcNsOr+hL/alEODq26StwlrnEDpxomFO+9YCdpNNEtUGHJbL562QR\nCNgDt3/grg2FPmYrwWIrf87osdetuSNBmxzQQ1e2P42AwRW/Bp39E/fyiSXjcbul\nt5sKw1ZpXQpBO7REJs9MQwtZwVCeatW40e6yfFVwZG9U2KjL87vCK4hryOi/UTw0\ni8fwbwDY0JoWnCuBk58koeQGwsb23zicR2O+IYV1QLNyZUpqeKU+Y/58GqfgYLDw\n/qATZ1ljgoy5wOs+WAaXNxIh+gMMcE0pW2w1j3eZ5DepL77ad/dtyFTh/LyP+8EW\nhYiqR55arL+PwwNx+Dd0u/cTc2K5y9/BVEun1Lg3S9RRlSNVtet83sWu7epaWhMd\nW1hNu89GhoUu2YmCer8xlv5CzCrdew2Mpurn+70Jh+TzF2lAo1mMLaSDd2NgmS+m\nApA8M2yEWkN6MFhKjr93tzhhzu9WONqVQlw3hYLu3PCsx+sgupVsYjSarYOIbLTe\nGuGnw4SqHfVu+T7sWpdf\n=JHul\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n",
        "payload": "tree 40d824f192f43e7550c98af4c376a4f950309837\nparent 35da507bb4e3e33ee12a0801c917478c5015a48d\nauthor Rob Woodgate <robwoodgate@users.noreply.github.com> 1779458455 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779458455 +0200\n\nfeat(mintinfo): add supportedMethods(op) to list usable mint/melt methods (#673)\n\n* feat(mintinfo): add supportedMethods(op) to list usable mint/melt methods\n\nAdds a convenience for discovering what a consumer can mint or melt with:\n`MintInfo.supportedMethods('mint' | 'melt')` returns the advertised method-unit\nsettings (SwapMethod[]), or [] when the operation is disabled.\n\nThis is the discovery counterpart to the existing point-check\n`supportsMintMeltMethod(op, method, unit)`. Unlike `isSupported(4|5).params`,\nit is operation-named and excludes disabled operations, so \"supported\" means\nusable. Kept on MintInfo only (no Wallet wrapper) to match the existing\nmethod-query surface and avoid a duplicate entry point.\n\n* docs(usage): add Inspect Mint Capabilities recipe for the method-query API\n\nNew usage page documenting how to discover what a mint supports via\nwallet.getMintInfo(): supportedMethods(op) to list usable mint/melt methods,\nsupportsMintMeltMethod(op, method, unit) for a single check, and isSupported(num)\nfor raw NUT support. Adds it to the usage index and cross-links it from the\nCreate Wallet recipe.",
