      },
      "message": "chore: document multi-major branch model and gate npm latest on LATEST_MAJOR (#670)\n\n* chore: document multi-major branch model and gate npm latest on LATEST_MAJOR\n\nEstablish the release machinery and docs for running several major lines in\nparallel ahead of v5 landing on main.\n\nversion.yml: introduce a workflow-level LATEST_MAJOR env var and key the npm\n`latest` dist-tag off it instead of a hardcoded major. Promoting a new major to\n`latest` is now a one-line, reviewed change; any major that is not LATEST_MAJOR\n(and is not a prerelease) falls through to `vN-lts` and can never accidentally\nbecome `latest`.\n\nDEVELOPER.md, CONTRIBUTING.md, AGENTS.md: rewrite the branching and release\nsections to be major-agnostic. main tracks the current major; each supported\nprior major is maintained on its own `vN-dev` LTS branch for fixes only.\nDocument the dist-tag rules, the LATEST_MAJOR knob, and a concise two-step\nmajor-transition cutover. The branch snapshot front-runs main to v5 so it is\ncorrect the moment the v5 stack merges.\n\n* docs: tidy npm dist-tags table in DEVELOPER.md",
